# FOR OPERATIONS AGAINST A HOSTED PROJECT ONLY. Values come from the Supabase
# dashboard: Settings -> API Keys. .env* is git-ignored (except this file).
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT DOES NOT NEED THIS FILE. `npm run dev` writes .env.local itself,
# from the stack it just started - copying keys by hand was the most common way to end
# up with a dev server pointed at nothing. It refuses to overwrite a .env.local that
# points anywhere other than 127.0.0.1, so if you are setting up a hosted operation
# here, `npm run dev` will leave your file alone rather than clobber it.

# Public by design - ships to every browser.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://wzzrxoslcwpyopdvvxmn.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Bypasses RLS. Never prefix with VITE_ (that would ship it to
# the browser), never commit it, never paste it into a chat window.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...

# OPTIONAL. A pepper for the login rate limiter's IP buckets, so auth_throttle stores
# hashes rather than addresses. If unset it falls back to SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY, which
# works fine - the only consequence is that rotating the secret key re-buckets whoever
# is mid-attempt, costing one 15-minute window of counting. Set it if you would rather
# the two were independent.
# AUTH_IP_PEPPER=

# OPTIONAL, and only for rehearsing the real email sender locally before deploying.
# Leave unset for normal development: the local stack captures mail at
# http://127.0.0.1:54324 and sends nothing. To use it, also uncomment [auth.email.smtp]
# in supabase/config.toml. The HOSTED project's SMTP is configured in the Supabase
# dashboard instead - see docs/EMAIL-SETUP.md.
# RESEND_SMTP_PASSWORD=

# LEAGUE EMAIL (issue #57). Server-side only, and NOT needed for local development:
# nothing is sent from a machine whose database is local, key or no key
# (server/email/resend.js). Set these in Netlify for the deployed site, and here only if
# you are running `npm run verify:notify` against the real sender.
#
# A DIFFERENT SENDING DOMAIN FROM THE MAGIC LINKS, on purpose. League mail is the kind
# people eventually mark as spam, and the complaint lands on the sending domain - which
# for sign-in mail is the only way anybody gets into this app. See docs/EMAIL-SETUP.md.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# NOTIFY_FROM=Pigskin Poker <league@notify.yourdomain.com>
#
# Signs the unsubscribe links in every league email. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Rotating it invalidates every unsubscribe link already sitting in an inbox.
# NOTIFY_SIGNING_SECRET=
#
# OPTIONAL. Where links in emails point. Netlify sets URL itself, so this is only for
# running scripts locally against the hosted sender.
# SITE_URL=https://pigskin.ballsohard.org
